<title>BELGIUM: Commission olive oil report again delayed.</title>
<headline>Commission olive oil report again delayed.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A European Commission report on options to reform the olive oil marketing regime, simplifying subsidies and curbing costly fraud, has been postponed by one week until January 29, Commission officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>They did not give a reason for the latest delay.</p>
<p>The report has already been postponed several times due to strong opposition from southern producing countries who fear it will lead to revenue losses and a decline in quality.</p>
</text>
